---
description: Require tests that assert observable behavior
alwaysApply: true
---

# Meaningful tests

A behavior change is incomplete until a test fails on the old behavior and passes on the new one. Assert an outcome: HTTP status and body, a `tenant_id` row, a policy reason, or a UI state.

Ship these with the feature: tenant isolation, TPO gate, wrong password and lockout, policy rejection reason, and one UI flow (login, apply, or approve).

Reject `expect(true).toBe(true)`, empty tests, "did not throw", snapshot-only tests, mocking the unit under test, production calls, and real secrets.

```ts
// BAD
expect(true).toBe(true);
// GOOD
expect(res.status).toBe(404);
expect(res.body.error).toBe("job_not_visible");
```
